acceptance_criteria: A real POSIX script with a missing interpreter fails as spawn_error while retaining platform exit code and stderr; Installed scripts deliberately emitting matching diagnostics or exiting127 remain assertion failures and commands are never rerun during classification; Lifecycle guidance negative controls explicitly pin the failing adapter revision and replay only the relevant assertion in an isolated tracker
parent: pm-gh1604
resolution: "Corroborate resolved POSIX script startup failures using a bounded shebang read and absent absolute interpreter, preserving native diagnostics and executed-child assertions. Pin lifecycle and interpreter negative controls to immutable failing source substitutions."
expected_result: Absent interpreters classify as spawn_error without rerunning commands; installed child failures retain assertion semantics; negative controls reproduce only their intended regression.
actual_result: "All110 linked tests pass, including real script failures and spoofed126/127 child diagnostics. Focused exact coverage is100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts. Three immutable-source replays prove their intended assertion failure, with setup/runtime failures distinguished. Typecheck, lint and docs checks pass; final hosted/review gates remain pre-merge requirements."
